column52:
I don't know whether to laugh or cry at some of these anecdotes.<p><i>As a final example, a buffer overflow checker flagged a bunch of errors of the form<p><pre><code>  unsigned p[4];
  ...
  p[4] = 1;
</code></pre>
"No, ANSI lets you write 1 past the end of the array."<p>After heated argument, the programmer said, "We'll have to agree to disagree." We could agree about the disagreement, though we couldn't quite comprehend it.</i>
